course: dictionary
lesson: 5928
title: Marshy ground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Marshy means soft and wet, like a marsh, so water lies on or just under the ground. When you step on marshy ground, your feet can sink in and squelch.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Many forced labourers died building it on marshy land.» The word land tells you what marshy describes: the ground. Building on that ground is the clue that it was not firm and dry.
explain: Use the swap test. Put soft and wet in place of marshy: «on soft, wet land» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Marshy is an adjective and can change: marshier and marshiest compare how wet the ground is. Marshy land is wet, marshier land is wetter, and the marshiest land is the wettest of all.
fact: Marshy means soft and wet, like a marsh.
fact: A marsh is a wetland where water lies on or just under the ground.
fact: «Marshy land» means ground that is soft and wet.
fact: Marshy has the forms marshier and marshiest, which compare how wet something is.
fact: Marshy is a useful word for geography and nature, where wetlands are studied.
exercise: «Many forced labourers died building it on marshy land.» What does marshy mean? | Very high and steep | *Soft and wet, with water on or under the ground | Warm and sunny | Hard and rocky like a mountain
exercise: Which word in this sentence tells you that marshy describes the ground? | many | building | *land | died
exercise: Ella says marshy means soft and sweet, like a marshmallow. What does marshy really mean? | Dry and dusty | Hard and shiny | Sweet and sticky | *Soft and wet, like a marsh
test: The hikers' boots sank into the marshy ground with every step. What does marshy mean here? | Covered in snow | Hard and rocky | *Soft and wet, with water under the ground | Hot and sandy
test: Which word is the right form to describe the wettest ground of all? | marshy | marshier | marshing | *marshiest
exam: Hal says marshy means dry and sandy, like a desert. What does marshy really mean? | *Soft and wet, like a marsh | Cold and icy | Tall and green | Dry and sandy like a desert
